# narration map — a visit is played on a map of the location
#
# The map is the narration's whole screen: LocationMap draws every area as a card inside its
# section's panel, the played member's token on the card they stand in, and on each card of ground
# already stood on a symbol for every kind of thing not yet looked at. On a first arrival only the
# yard is visited, its neighbours are seen (named, dimmed) and the rest is unknown: the Test Den,
# two ways off past the wood, reads ??? and must not be named. The map has no legend and no footer
# button; the way out is the glyph in its margin.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

expect Test Yard
expect ???
expect-not Test Den
expect-not [ LEAVE ]
expect-state where exit=LEAVE

# Nothing is observed on arrival: what stands in the yard is on its card as symbols, by kind.
expect-state trees ""
regions
expect-state noetic points=3/3

# The arrow keys pan it. The section's tab is off the left edge while the view is centred on the
# yard, and comes into view as the map moves right under it.
expect-not Test Grounds
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
key Left
wait
expect Test Grounds

# The way out is a click on its glyph, from anywhere on the map.
click exit
wait mode WorldView 60
quit
